Bundled boundary data
=====================

SignalK Starlink Offshore ships pre-converted, compressed world datasets for
three layers used to classify the vessel's maritime zone:

  1. territorial sea  - Marine Regions (VLIZ) Territorial Seas (12NM) v4
  2. internal waters  - Marine Regions (VLIZ) World Internal Waters v4
  3. land             - Natural Earth 10m Admin 0 Countries

Internal waters is what distinguishes a bay inside a state's straight
baselines (e.g. Cartagena harbour) from the territorial sea seaward of them;
land is Natural Earth because Marine Regions publishes no standalone land
layer (their EEZ+Land union cannot separate land from sea).

